   "id": "spcpt_8MpvS5pnYkf9QswF",
   "name": "FDP Conversions",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "FDP conversions"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I convert from a percentage to a decimal?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Divide by 100** (move digits two places to the right)\n\n  - 6% as a decimal is 6 ÷ 100 = 0.06\n  - 40% as a decimal is 40 ÷ 100 = 0.4\n  - 350% as a decimal is 350 ÷ 100 = 3.5\n  - 0.2% as a decimal is 0.2 ÷ 100 = 0.002"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I convert from a decimal to a percentage?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- **Multiply by 100** (move digits two places to the left and add a % sign)\n\n  - 0.35 as a percentage is  0.35 × 100 = 35%\n  - 1.32 as a percentage is 1.32 × 100 = 132%\n  - 0.004 as a percentage is 0.004 × 100 = 0.4%"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I convert from a decimal to a fraction?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- If it has o**ne decimal place**, write the digits over **10**\n\n  - 0.3 is $\\frac{3}{10}$\n  - 1.1 is $\\frac{11}{10}$\n- If it has **two decimal places**, write the digits over **100**\n\n  - 0.07 is $\\frac{7}{100}$\n  - 0.13 is  $\\frac{13}{100}$\n  - 30.01 is  $\\frac{3001}{100}$\n- If it has ***n***** decimal places**, write the digits over **10**<sup>***n***</sup>\n\n  - 0.513 is $\\frac{513}{1000}$\n  - 0.0007 is  $\\frac{7}{10000}$\n- Learn **simple recurring decimals** as fractions\n\n  - 0.33333… = `0.3 with dot on top`  is  $\\frac{1}{3}$\n  - 0.66666… =  `0.6 with dot on top` is  $\\frac{2}{3}$\n- **Whole numbers** can be written as fractions by writing them over **1**\n\n  - 5 is $\\frac{5}{1}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I convert from a percentage to a fraction?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Write the **percentage over 100**\n\n  - 37% is $\\frac{37}{100}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I convert from a fraction to a decimal?"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2025/12/32468-9570-order-by-size-notes-fig2a.png",
   "file": "assets/ac4307edafa2-32468-9570-order-by-size-notes-fig2a.png",
   "alt": "converting between fractions and decimals",
   "caption": ""
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Fractions written **over powers of 10** are quicker\n\n  - $\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{6}{10}$ which is 0.6\n  - $\\frac{7}{20}=\\frac{35}{100}$ which is 0.35\n  - $\\frac{1}{500}=\\frac{2}{1000}$ which is 0.002"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I convert from a fraction to a percentage?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Change fractions into **decimals** then **multiply by 100**\n\n  - $\\frac{4}{5}=\\frac{8}{10}$ which is 0.8 as a decimal, which is 0.8 × 100 = 80%"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "A calculator can be used to check conversions between fractions and decimals (even if the question says to show working without a calculator)."
  }
 ]
}